    "result_text": "All changes are complete and the test suite is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: fiscal-year basis for date-derived values\n\nThe fiscal year starts **1 July** and is named by the calendar year it ends in (Australian convention), so a July\u2013December date reports the *next* calendar year's fiscal year (e.g. `2026-08-10` \u2192 FY2027 \u2192 `FY27`).\n\n**New shared utility** \u2014 `model/FiscalYear.java`:\n- `of(LocalDate)` \u2192 the fiscal year integer (`month >= 7 ? year + 1 : year`)\n- `label(LocalDate)` \u2192 the `FY<YY>` string\n\n**Membership identifier's year segment now uses the fiscal year** (previously calendar year, `getYear() % 100`):\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 `membershipNumber` expression, plus added `FiscalYear` to the mapper `imports`.\n- `rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java` \u2014 the duplicated membership-number builder used in the audit log, kept consistent.\n\n**Tenure now counts elapsed fiscal years, not 365-day windows** \u2014 `model/MembershipLevel.java`:\n- `tenureDays` (via `ChronoUnit.DAYS`) replaced with `tenureFiscalYears` = `FiscalYear.of(now) - FiscalYear.of(registrationDate)`.\n- The `+3` bonus now applies for **more than 1** elapsed fiscal year (preserving the original \"more than one year\" threshold semantics).\n\n**New `fiscalYear` response field** \u2014 `resources/openapi.yml`:\n- Added the `fiscalYear` schema property (`FY<YY>`) on the owner DTO, mapped in `OwnerMapper` via `FiscalYear.label(...)`.\n- Updated `membershipNumber` and `membershipPoints` descriptions to match the new fiscal-year semantics.\n\n**Verification:** `./mvnw -o test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. The new acceptance test `coreReturnsFiscalYear` (asserts the response's `fiscalYear` matches `FY\\d{2}`) passes, and the audit log confirms the membership number now derives its year segment from the fiscal year.",
